# Review-driven Java practices

When a reviewer comments, treat the comment as the next standard. Apply it
instead of classifying it as optional polish, unless it contradicts an
approved `SPEC.md` decision.

- Descriptive names; no single-letter loop indices or vague `value` parameters.
- Focused methods and types. Independent validation/discount policies are
  separate composable units, not one registry of lambdas.
- Constructors and factories reject invalid state. Do not leave public value
  types as unvalidated field assignments.
- Canonicalize a field in one owner (entity or directory), not two helpers.
- Tests use separate `// Arrange`, `// Act`, `// Assert` comments, one
  behavior per test, and observable outcomes rather than reflection on
  modifiers. Assert immutability on every returned bucket.
- Do not store personal email, secrets, or environment data in the repo.
